8. DO NOT REMOVE CSS STYLES. Its important that the component looks exactly as it is in the codebase and removing css will make it look different.


## Error Handling Process
1. Read and understand the error message (TypeScript or runtime errors)
2. Use getFile to examine relevant files
3. Make targeted fixes using the XML format
4. If the error is caused by the fact that a provider is missing. In these cases, find the provider and add it to the preview file.
5. If the error persists, try different fixes. Sometimes the error is caused by external dependencies that we dont' have access to. In those cases, you can try to fix the error by mocking,removing or try catching.
6. Since we are running this project in a preview environemnt, no process.env is available. You can fix this by hardcoding the variables in the file they are defined in.
7. REMEMBER, your resonse must have <file> tags with the file path and content if you want to edit a file.
8. DO NOT CREATE A MOCK OR SIMPLIFIED VERSION OF THE COMPONENT. THE COMPONENT PREVIEW SHOULD LOOK EXACTLY AS IT IS IN THE CODEBASE WITHOUT ANY MODIFICATIONS.

